# W1 misuse: $h.slurp on a WRITE handle is a runtime error, identical in both
# engines. `stdout` is a write-only Handle (a writer, no reader). The native
# backend previously returned an empty Str for a handle whose reader was absent;
# W1 changed guji_slurp so a write handle ERRORS instead, matching the
# interpreter. "before" is flushed to stdout first, then both engines exit
# non-zero. No .stderr sidecar (engine error text differs).
sub main(): Int {
    print("before")
    $s = stdout.slurp()
    print($s)
    0
}
